assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable. A single operational fixture (FX-B1) on the bound fx-b1 profile can show the following, with retained command, exit status, raw observations and actual readback:
- identity, order and timestamps persist across a supervised kill/restart;
- the five anomaly classes are detected;
- retention and the queue survive the restart;
- attention-producer consumption observes the receipts;
- pre- and post-restart observations reconcile without loss.
The custody model has the verifier retrieve the exact candidate SHA in a fresh worktree, so one independent verdict on 'predicate proven on the bound target, labelled as proof-only, no observer data read' is meaningful. The proof plan requires fixture commands, expected outcomes and the evidence schema to be pinned before implementation, even though no acceptance probes are pre-listed. The verifier should confirm operational (not local-substitute) readback, the absence of any observer-service reads, and disjointness from real factory state.
